# Keep a single line ending in the repository so scripts, config snippets and
# docs behave identically on every machine.
# Windows PowerShell 5.1 and PowerShell 7+ both run LF-only .ps1 files fine.
* text=auto eol=lf

*.ps1  text eol=lf
*.md   text eol=lf
*.toml text eol=lf
*.json text eol=lf

# Batch files are stored byte-for-byte with CRLF endings (-text = no conversion).
# cmd.exe is unreliable with LF-only .cmd/.bat files, and normalising through the
# index means the archive/checkout result depends on host settings - so the bytes
# committed here are exactly the bytes Windows will run.
*.cmd  -text
*.bat  -text

*.png binary
*.gif binary
*.jpg binary
*.zip binary
